                  <bindingDesc resp="#BCBB">
                     <binding notAfter="1500" notBefore="1400">
                        <p>A composite binding, where the boards seem earlier than the leather:</p>
                        <p>15th century, <placeName key="place_1000080">Italian</placeName> (contemporary with manuscript?, for the <orgName key="org_136227334">Dominican nuns of Corpus Domini, Venice</orgName>): wood boards, with traces of two fore-edge clasps present in nails and grooves under the leather; edges gilt, possible traces of gauffering.</p>
                     </binding>
                     <binding notAfter="1600" notBefore="1500">
                        <p>16th century?, <placeName key="place_1000080">Italian</placeName>: dark brown leather, simply blind-tooled with double lines around the edges and also forming a large blank diamond-shaped panel on each cover; no allowance for the boards’ clasp fittings.</p>
                     </binding>
                     <binding notAfter="1800" notBefore="1700">
                        <p>18th century, <placeName key="place_1000080">Italian</placeName>: paste-downs and flyleaves of carta bassanese added for Jacopo Soranzo, 
                           whose label is at top of spine
                           </p>
                     </binding>
                  </bindingDesc>
               </physDesc>
               <history>
                  <origin>
