                  <provenance>In the Calendar the 'Dedicatione ecclesie' is on 12 July</provenance> 
                  
                  <provenance>Cf. <ref target="https://medieval.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/catalog/manuscript_2903">MS. Canon Liturg. 212</ref></provenance>
                     
                  <provenance>St Peter, Dominican and Martyr, of Milan, is specially honoured (29th April and 7th May), 
                     and in the Litany is St Marina of Venice</provenance>
                    
                  <provenance>Among the devotions of the Virgin is a prayer with (187v) 'per intercessionem beatiss. Marci apostoli 
                  et evangeliste tui et b. Stephani martiris tui atque beatissimi Jeronimi et beatorum Cosme et Damiani necnon et sanctiss. patris nostri s. Dominici et 
                  s. Thome de Aquino...'</provenance>
                  
                  <provenance><orgName role="fmo" key="org_136227334">Dominican nuns of Corpus Domini, Venice</orgName></provenance>
                  
                  <provenance><persName key="person_2384880" role="fmo">Matteo Luigi Canonici (1727– <hi rend="italic">c</hi>. 1806)</persName></provenance>
                  <provenance notAfter="1807" resp="#SC">Following Canonici's death, the collection passed to his brother, <persName key="person_446" role="fmo">Giuseppe Canonici</persName>, and 
                     then to Canonici's nephew, <persName role="fmo" key="person_431">Giovanni Perissinotti</persName>, in 1807 following Giuseppe Canonici's death</provenance>
                  <acquisition when="1817">Bought by the Bodleian Library in 1817 from Giovanni Perissinotti. On the purchase, see <ref target="https://digital.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/collections/canonici/">Digital Bodleian</ref></acquisition>
                  
